26
00:01:43,130 --> 00:01:45,460
Let me settle this with you.

27
00:01:43,190 --> 00:01:46,370
[Previously on KNOT]

28
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:48,700
I love you, Phatsa.

29
00:01:50,060 --> 00:01:50,590
Hello?

30
00:01:50,610 --> 00:01:51,150
Mr. Phatsa!

31
00:01:51,150 --> 00:01:51,810
Mr. Phatsa!

32
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:53,259
Nurse!

33
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:54,660
Nakhun!

34
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:01,930
I'm here to apologize

35
00:02:05,800 --> 00:02:07,800
for biting Phatsa.

36
00:02:12,660 --> 00:02:15,390
I really never wanted things
to turn out this way.

37
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:17,410
At the time, I...

38
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:21,930
I just lost control of my instincts.

39
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:25,500
You couldn't control yourself?

40
00:02:26,329 --> 00:02:27,130
Yes.

41
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:31,420
An Alpha
who couldn't even control himself,

42
00:02:32,130 --> 00:02:33,460
and yet he made my son

43
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:35,560
enter into a bond with him.

44
00:02:37,860 --> 00:02:38,660
Dad.

45
00:02:38,860 --> 00:02:40,660
Then what am I supposed to think?

46
00:02:43,930 --> 00:02:46,390
Am I supposed to
treat this like an accident?

47
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:47,820
It wasn't an accident.

48
00:02:51,730 --> 00:02:54,300
I don't expect you to understand.

49
00:02:57,930 --> 00:02:59,860
Because no matter how I explain it,

50
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:02,760
what Phatsa went through

51
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:07,760
has already happened.

52
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:11,160
But I believe

53
00:03:12,080 --> 00:03:15,270
everything happened between me and Phatsa

54
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:18,900
because we're soulmates.

55
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:28,000
Soulmates?

56
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:30,730
Yes.

57
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:34,520
The attraction between me and Phatsa

58
00:03:34,660 --> 00:03:36,360
is far beyond what's normal.

59
00:03:38,630 --> 00:03:42,329
Even our instincts are harder to control
than before.

60
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:45,900
So?

61
00:03:46,730 --> 00:03:48,060
You want me

62
00:03:49,060 --> 00:03:51,060
to just pretend you never bit my son?

63
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:52,760
No.

64
00:03:54,130 --> 00:03:56,060
I'm not using this as an excuse.

65
00:03:58,060 --> 00:03:59,590
I just want to tell the truth

66
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:01,360
and take responsibility

67
00:04:01,830 --> 00:04:02,900
for what I did.

68
00:04:03,710 --> 00:04:04,710
Responsibility?

69
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,280
Do you know

70
00:04:11,260 --> 00:04:13,230
what it means to bite an Omega?

71
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:15,430
Do you know

72
00:04:16,630 --> 00:04:18,760
what my son is going to face from now on?

73
00:04:19,510 --> 00:04:20,200
I know.

74
00:04:21,529 --> 00:04:22,630
Can you bear it?

75
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:27,320
If Phatsa loses something because of me,

76
00:04:28,730 --> 00:04:30,760
I'll take full responsibility.

77
00:04:36,060 --> 00:04:37,520
That's easy for you to say.

78
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:40,060
I'm not just saying.

79
00:04:41,130 --> 00:04:42,260
I'm saying it as a man

80
00:04:42,600 --> 00:04:44,530
who doesn't run from his problems.

81
00:04:45,460 --> 00:04:47,110
Mr. Chakjetsada,

82
00:04:47,130 --> 00:04:50,360
my boss isn't here to negotiate today.

83
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:54,830
He just wants to
explain things to you in person,

84
00:04:54,830 --> 00:04:55,760
and reassure you

85
00:04:55,930 --> 00:04:59,060
that Phatsa is safe and sound.

86
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:06,340
Dad.

87
00:05:08,460 --> 00:05:10,500
Nakhun really didn't mean it.

88
00:05:11,930 --> 00:05:13,730
And you're still defending him?

89
00:05:15,240 --> 00:05:17,170
I'm not defending anyone.

90
00:05:18,560 --> 00:05:19,360
I just want Dad

91
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,400
to hear him out first.

92
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:34,130
I know you're mad at me now.

93
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:38,800
No matter what you think of me,

94
00:05:41,400 --> 00:05:43,360
I won't deny it.

95
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:49,730
I'll never abandon Phatsa.

96
00:05:52,130 --> 00:05:54,200
I won't believe everything you say.

97
00:05:56,330 --> 00:05:58,190
But since you stood in front of me,

98
00:05:58,960 --> 00:05:59,960
bowed to me,

99
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:02,700
and admitted your fault,

100
00:06:07,730 --> 00:06:08,990
I'm willing to listen.

101
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:19,090
Thank you.

102
00:06:21,880 --> 00:06:22,880
But don't think

103
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,000
I'll hand my son over to you that easily.

104
00:06:27,760 --> 00:06:28,560
Dad.

105
00:06:31,430 --> 00:06:31,900
Yes,

106
00:06:33,200 --> 00:06:34,000
I understand.

107
00:06:59,260 --> 00:06:59,560
Hey.

108
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:01,800
Is he always like this?

109
00:07:02,290 --> 00:07:03,200
Yes.

110
00:07:22,230 --> 00:07:23,730
All along,

111
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,200
I've done my best to take care of Phatsa,

112
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:31,860
like a man

113
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:36,530
taking care of the most important person
in his life.

114
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:42,700
Before,

115
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:46,060
maybe it's because of instincts,

116
00:07:47,830 --> 00:07:49,300
or the bond.

117
00:07:56,659 --> 00:07:57,730
But now,

118
00:08:00,400 --> 00:08:02,930
I take care of Phatsa
not only because of duty.

119
00:08:04,530 --> 00:08:05,900
I stay by his side

120
00:08:06,900 --> 00:08:08,300
not because of instinct.

121
00:08:18,300 --> 00:08:20,130
I truly love Phatsa.

122
00:08:23,130 --> 00:08:28,210
If you ask me

123
00:08:28,230 --> 00:08:32,950
what I plan to do with Phatsa from now on,

124
00:08:35,960 --> 00:08:39,400
my answer is: I'm going to marry him,
with full ceremony and honor,

125
00:08:39,400 --> 00:08:40,929
in a way worthy of Phatsa.

126
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:44,460
Worthy of the fact that he is my beloved.

127
00:08:45,900 --> 00:08:46,860
No father

128
00:08:48,860 --> 00:08:50,590
would easily hand over his son.

129
00:08:52,030 --> 00:08:53,850
Especially to the man who bit his son

130
00:08:53,850 --> 00:08:55,250
on the first day they met.

131
00:08:58,260 --> 00:09:00,250
No matter how nice you put it,

132
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:02,660
what happened has happened.

133
00:09:03,460 --> 00:09:07,630
I won't let my son go with you so easily.

134
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:11,660
Phatsa,

135
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,260
you have to move back home.

136
00:09:15,700 --> 00:09:16,500
Do you hear me?

137
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:34,760
Dad,

138
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:38,860
please listen to me first.

139
00:09:40,530 --> 00:09:42,930
Ever since the day
I found out I was an Omega,

140
00:09:45,030 --> 00:09:46,560
I've been completely lost.

141
00:09:48,560 --> 00:09:50,260
I didn't know how to face it.

142
00:09:51,800 --> 00:09:53,400
or how to accept this world.

143
00:09:54,560 --> 00:09:57,200
I felt depressed and angry.

144
00:09:59,730 --> 00:10:02,760
I always felt like all of this
was forced on me.

145
00:10:04,630 --> 00:10:05,760
Whether my identity

146
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:07,960
or the bond,

147
00:10:10,060 --> 00:10:10,760
it's like

148
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:13,500
my life was never my own choice.

149
00:10:21,260 --> 00:10:25,930
But someone changed everything.

150
00:10:29,130 --> 00:10:33,300
That person is Nakhun.

151
00:10:41,560 --> 00:10:43,560
He took care of not just my body,

152
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,500
but my heart.

153
00:10:50,330 --> 00:10:51,130
Dad,

154
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:53,760
I love him.

155
00:10:57,860 --> 00:11:00,200
Can you try to accept him?

156
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:04,760
And there's one more thing

157
00:11:05,930 --> 00:11:07,900
I want to tell you in person.

158
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:11,560
What's it?

159
00:11:17,860 --> 00:11:18,800
Phatsa and I

160
00:11:20,800 --> 00:11:23,260
have already completed
the permanent bond.

161
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:27,530
And I've also bonded with Phatsa.

162
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:32,990
Why did you say it in front of my dad?

163
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:36,130
What are you talking about?

164
00:11:37,760 --> 00:11:39,730
You'll have a grandchild soon.

165
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:46,460
How could you say something like that
in front of my dad?

166
00:11:47,960 --> 00:11:49,690
Because my son pleaded for you,

167
00:11:53,460 --> 00:11:55,300
if you want to marry my son,

168
00:11:56,560 --> 00:11:58,690
the bride price will be astronomical.

169
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:02,690
I'll demand so much
that you'll be left with nothing.

170
00:12:03,400 --> 00:12:04,500
What do you think?

171
00:12:06,130 --> 00:12:07,730
As long as you are satisfied,

172
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,400
I'm willing to give it to you.

173
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,560
Don't act tough in front of me.

174
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:21,160
I'm serious.

175
00:12:26,360 --> 00:12:28,420
Dad, go ahead and name a higher price.

176
00:12:30,930 --> 00:12:32,800
If this is what you're worth,

177
00:12:35,960 --> 00:12:37,130
I can afford it.

178
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:45,960
These two kids are really...

179
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:49,560
That's just how they are.

180
00:13:22,960 --> 00:13:24,100
Mr. Nakhun,

181
00:13:26,200 --> 00:13:27,930
it's time to take the medicine.

182
00:13:36,760 --> 00:13:37,560
Phatsa.

183
00:13:42,960 --> 00:13:43,760
Phatsa.

184
00:13:45,560 --> 00:13:46,560
Where's Phatsa?

185
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:48,760
Wasn't he here just now?

186
00:13:49,860 --> 00:13:51,160
Calm down.

187
00:13:52,660 --> 00:13:53,800
That

188
00:13:54,700 --> 00:13:56,260
was four hours ago.

189
00:13:56,730 --> 00:13:59,260
The medicine took effect
and you fell asleep.

190
00:14:07,460 --> 00:14:08,860
Then where's Phatsa?

191
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:11,960
Don't tell me he abandoned me.

192
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:14,360
Phatsa didn't abandon you.

193
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:17,300
It was your father-in-law,

194
00:14:18,560 --> 00:14:19,760
Mr. Chakjetsada.

195
00:14:20,530 --> 00:14:23,330
When you fell asleep,
his expression changed in an instant.

196
00:14:23,330 --> 00:14:26,960
He said the wedding hasn't been held yet,

197
00:14:27,360 --> 00:14:29,470
so he couldn't let his son stay here

198
00:14:29,490 --> 00:14:31,290
to spend the night with an Alpha.

199
00:14:31,660 --> 00:14:33,600
So he took him back home.

200
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:36,560
What?

201
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,400
Didn't we already agree?

202
00:14:40,820 --> 00:14:41,620
Sila,

203
00:14:42,930 --> 00:14:44,930
how can you let him take my wife away?

204
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:47,220
Don't forget you're a bodyguard!

205
00:14:47,730 --> 00:14:49,990
Who would dare stop your father-in-law?

206
00:14:50,700 --> 00:14:53,700
He exerted some pressure as an elder,

207
00:14:54,530 --> 00:14:57,300
and then brought up Phatsa's reputation.

208
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:00,000
I had no choice but to let them go.

209
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:03,100
Besides, Phatsa was exhausted
and had fallen asleep by then.

210
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:04,100
Get the car ready.

211
00:15:04,300 --> 00:15:05,550
I'm going to bring Phatsa back.

212
00:15:05,550 --> 00:15:06,550
Please calm down.

213
00:15:07,260 --> 00:15:08,660
Please lie down and rest.

214
00:15:09,360 --> 00:15:11,360
The wound has just been stitched up.

215
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:13,260
No.

216
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:15,430
I need to bring Phatsa back.

217
00:15:15,800 --> 00:15:17,530
You should get some rest first.

218
00:15:18,700 --> 00:15:19,910
I can't believe

219
00:15:19,930 --> 00:15:21,820
a True Alpha like you

220
00:15:21,850 --> 00:15:23,860
is this clingy with his wife.

221
00:15:25,530 --> 00:15:26,660
Don't be sarcastic.

222
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:30,020
You're not me. You don't understand.

223
00:15:33,190 --> 00:15:34,170
How about this?

224
00:15:34,190 --> 00:15:37,740
I'll take you to Phatsa tomorrow morning.

225
00:15:41,530 --> 00:15:42,860
Get some rest now.

226
00:15:44,810 --> 00:15:45,780
Be careful.

227
00:16:24,300 --> 00:16:25,700
Is everyone okay?

228
00:16:27,160 --> 00:16:30,100
Yes, everything is fine.

229
00:16:33,100 --> 00:16:34,360
What about Saengnuea?

230
00:16:38,260 --> 00:16:39,960
He confessed everything,

231
00:16:40,800 --> 00:16:42,730
including what happened with Tim,

232
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:45,030
and the plan to destroy the bar,

233
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:48,760
and the fact that
he fabricated the human trafficking case.

234
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:50,330
His hatred

235
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:54,060
has been driving him
to do these crazy things.

236
00:16:55,300 --> 00:16:57,730
He lived in the fire he lit himself.

237
00:16:58,690 --> 00:17:02,590
In the end, he was burned by the fire.

238
00:17:04,460 --> 00:17:06,160
Hatred is truly terrifying.

239
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:11,260
So where is Saengnuea now?

240
00:17:12,960 --> 00:17:14,950
That doesn't matter.

241
00:17:14,980 --> 00:17:18,730
What really gives us a headache
is the trouble that comes after.

242
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:23,099
What trouble? Isn't everything resolved?

243
00:17:26,130 --> 00:17:29,190
It's all because of
our troublemaking little brother.

244
00:17:29,560 --> 00:17:30,530
Back then, Saengnuea

245
00:17:30,530 --> 00:17:32,930
tried to go into heat
to force me to bite him.

246
00:17:33,130 --> 00:17:34,970
But then Naphitch

247
00:17:34,990 --> 00:17:37,450
suddenly rushed out
and stood in front of me,

248
00:17:37,700 --> 00:17:38,830
and he bit Saengnuea,

249
00:17:38,830 --> 00:17:40,490
entering into a bond with him.

250
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:42,600
What?

251
00:17:44,060 --> 00:17:46,060
You bit Saengnuea?

252
00:17:47,630 --> 00:17:51,060
Do you know what entering a bond means?

253
00:17:53,980 --> 00:17:54,950
I know.

254
00:17:57,230 --> 00:17:59,570
But if I hadn't done it,

255
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:02,060
Nakhin and Ongsa
would have been finished.

256
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:05,440
And if I'd let him be,

257
00:18:05,470 --> 00:18:07,700
he would have come back to hurt us.

258
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:11,360
I'll take responsibility

259
00:18:12,600 --> 00:18:14,600
for his hatred to the very end.

260
00:18:34,060 --> 00:18:36,880
Eat your food.

261
00:18:36,900 --> 00:18:39,860
You'll need the strength to keep sulking.

262
00:18:41,560 --> 00:18:47,560
Eat it or not,
no one's going to feel sorry for you.

263
00:18:48,660 --> 00:18:50,610
The bite mark on your neck

264
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,430
is an invisible chain

265
00:18:54,400 --> 00:18:56,200
binding you to Naphitch.

266
00:18:57,900 --> 00:18:59,730
No matter how far you go,

267
00:19:00,930 --> 00:19:03,860
you'll crawl back
to the person who bit you in the end.

268
00:19:05,060 --> 00:19:06,360
Get used to it.

269
00:19:06,730 --> 00:19:07,530
Trust me.

270
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:33,010
[HEINRICH MEDICAL CENTER]

271
00:19:34,630 --> 00:19:35,640
Phatsa.

272
00:19:40,730 --> 00:19:42,820
[HEINRICH MEDICAL CENTER]

273
00:19:44,660 --> 00:19:46,460
How could it be Phatsa?

274
00:19:47,300 --> 00:19:49,700
Sir, the test results have been confirmed.

275
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:53,330
Phatsa is a Pure Omega.

276
00:19:54,930 --> 00:19:55,760
Impossible.

277
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:02,260
What's wrong?

278
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:07,600
I know

279
00:20:07,620 --> 00:20:09,730
who that Pure Omega is now.

280
00:20:12,100 --> 00:20:12,900
Who is it?

281
00:20:14,830 --> 00:20:15,630
Phatsa.

282
00:20:16,110 --> 00:20:16,910
Phatsa!

283
00:20:18,960 --> 00:20:20,330
I never imagined

284
00:20:21,100 --> 00:20:24,200
that the person
we searched this whole city for

285
00:20:24,560 --> 00:20:26,490
has been right beside us all along.

286
00:20:27,630 --> 00:20:29,820
So everything that happened before

287
00:20:30,330 --> 00:20:31,990
is starting to make sense now.

288
00:20:32,760 --> 00:20:35,020
Don't you dare set your sights on Phatsa.

289
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:37,890
The more I learn about him,

290
00:20:39,900 --> 00:20:42,460
the less I'll let him slip away.

291
00:20:50,600 --> 00:20:51,800
Mr. Chawe,

292
00:20:53,530 --> 00:20:55,390
please step outside for a moment.

293
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:12,620
You can't accept Phatsa

294
00:21:12,650 --> 00:21:14,760
just because he's a Pure Omega.

295
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:20,740
Do you really know him?

296
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:26,710
It's precisely because I know him
that I'm telling you all this.

297
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:31,180
You should look at
people's good qualities more,

298
00:21:31,210 --> 00:21:34,500
instead of his status and bloodline.

299
00:21:34,960 --> 00:21:38,450
Phatsa is cheerful, brave,

300
00:21:38,470 --> 00:21:41,760
adorable, and he loves Nakhun
with all his heart.

301
00:21:44,530 --> 00:21:45,400
What happened?

302
00:21:48,610 --> 00:21:50,180
He's the only one

303
00:21:50,200 --> 00:21:53,290
who dared to teach Naphitch
to become a better person.

304
00:21:54,260 --> 00:21:56,240
He does housework and works hard.

305
00:21:56,260 --> 00:21:58,040
He never takes advantage of others.

306
00:21:58,040 --> 00:21:59,040
Even if Phatsa

307
00:21:59,060 --> 00:22:00,260
weren't a Pure Omega,

308
00:22:00,260 --> 00:22:04,000
I would still gladly accept him
as my son-in-law.

309
00:22:04,630 --> 00:22:07,250
You should also think about

310
00:22:07,270 --> 00:22:09,200
the matter of Nakhin and Ongsa now!

311
00:22:09,220 --> 00:22:10,860
No matter what you think,

312
00:22:12,050 --> 00:22:13,820
I will make sure

313
00:22:13,850 --> 00:22:15,690
Nakhin and Ongsa

314
00:22:15,710 --> 00:22:17,890
end up together.

315
00:22:21,600 --> 00:22:23,150
What a pity.

316
00:22:37,300 --> 00:22:38,100
What?

317
00:22:38,800 --> 00:22:40,700
Nakhin is a True Alpha.

318
00:22:40,950 --> 00:22:43,550
He was supposed
to be matched with a Pure Omega.

319
00:22:43,940 --> 00:22:46,170
Then think about the past

320
00:22:46,200 --> 00:22:48,930
when you were forced into marriage
by the elders!

321
00:22:53,730 --> 00:22:55,860
Don't let history repeat itself.

322
00:22:57,680 --> 00:22:59,520
Children have the right to choose.

323
00:22:59,520 --> 00:23:01,780
They have the right to choose who to love.

324
00:23:10,130 --> 00:23:13,800
So this is how much
Mom has suffered all this time.

325
00:23:17,760 --> 00:23:19,300
We knew Mom didn't love Dad,

326
00:23:21,300 --> 00:23:24,300
but we never knew
she'd been enduring it for this long.

327
00:23:26,060 --> 00:23:27,460
Mom never said anything.

328
00:23:28,530 --> 00:23:31,330
So no one ever knew
she'd been carrying it all alone.

329
00:23:31,330 --> 00:23:33,530
She has been carrying it all by herself.

330
00:23:34,040 --> 00:23:40,960
As for Naphitch,

331
00:23:41,710 --> 00:23:43,470
I've never treated him as an outsider.

332
00:23:43,470 --> 00:23:44,330
He's a member

333
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:45,960
of the Devathitirat family.

334
00:23:46,730 --> 00:23:47,920
He's already

335
00:23:47,950 --> 00:23:51,730
entered into a bond with Saengnuea.

336
00:23:52,300 --> 00:23:54,690
Even if that Omega is the one

337
00:23:54,710 --> 00:23:56,600
who destroyed our family,

338
00:23:58,500 --> 00:24:01,200
Naphitch chose to

339
00:24:01,230 --> 00:24:03,260
bind that demon to himself

340
00:24:03,260 --> 00:24:04,860
to protect his brothers.

341
00:24:05,560 --> 00:24:09,130
It means he's grown up.

342
00:24:09,760 --> 00:24:11,380
No matter how we have to face

343
00:24:11,410 --> 00:24:13,670
the mistakes Saengnuea made from now on,

344
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:17,490
I will stand by Naphitch's side

345
00:24:17,510 --> 00:24:19,160
as his mother.

346
00:24:29,600 --> 00:24:32,360
Mom is so cool!

347
00:24:41,640 --> 00:24:44,670
You handled that beautifully,

348
00:24:46,640 --> 00:24:47,440
as expected of

349
00:24:49,090 --> 00:24:51,230
my wife.

350
00:24:52,360 --> 00:24:56,100
This is what a mother should do.
It's also what I must do.

351
00:25:04,730 --> 00:25:08,360
And there's one more thing
I'd like to ask of you.

352
00:25:18,500 --> 00:25:20,900
Please sign the divorce papers.

353
00:25:24,500 --> 00:25:27,000
This is something
I should have done a long time ago.

354
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:29,420
I've been waiting for this day
for a long time.

355
00:25:29,420 --> 00:25:30,680
It's time.

356
00:25:49,300 --> 00:25:50,960
Mom, have you really decided?

357
00:25:51,400 --> 00:25:53,260
I've been certain for a long time.

358
00:25:53,360 --> 00:25:55,930
But today, I finally made up my mind.

359
00:25:57,060 --> 00:25:58,930
You don't have to go this far.

360
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:01,380
Yes, I do.

361
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:03,870
If I keep silent,

362
00:26:03,900 --> 00:26:05,630
then you will only ever live the lives

363
00:26:05,630 --> 00:26:07,730
others chose for you.

364
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:16,760
Naphitch,

365
00:26:18,800 --> 00:26:24,330
I want to tell you this
in front of everyone.

366
00:26:24,830 --> 00:26:26,100
To me,

367
00:26:26,500 --> 00:26:29,120
you're

368
00:26:29,140 --> 00:26:30,700
Nakhun and Nakhin's younger brother.

369
00:26:30,700 --> 00:26:32,860
And you're my son, too.

370
00:26:38,400 --> 00:26:39,200
You...

371
00:26:41,400 --> 00:26:42,200
Mom.

372
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:49,360
No matter what happened,

373
00:26:51,330 --> 00:26:52,540
you will always

374
00:26:52,560 --> 00:26:54,020
be a member of this family.

375
00:26:55,500 --> 00:26:56,700
I will never let you

376
00:26:56,730 --> 00:26:58,330
bear this burden alone.

377
00:27:20,130 --> 00:27:21,890
You're right.

378
00:27:21,910 --> 00:27:24,110
Naphitch is also a child of this family.

379
00:27:25,380 --> 00:27:29,650
From now on,
leave the matters in this family to me.

380
00:27:29,680 --> 00:27:31,480
I'll take care of them properly.

381
00:27:32,860 --> 00:27:36,160
I'll help you too.

382
00:27:39,800 --> 00:27:41,930
Everything I did today was for all of you.

383
00:27:41,930 --> 00:27:43,260
I don't regret any of it.

384
00:27:53,620 --> 00:27:55,310
I really didn't expect

385
00:27:57,850 --> 00:28:00,990
you guys to go this far.

386
00:28:16,660 --> 00:28:18,500
What happened next?

387
00:28:19,510 --> 00:28:21,650
Simply put,

388
00:28:21,670 --> 00:28:22,890
right now,

389
00:28:22,920 --> 00:28:25,880
the Devathitirat family
is in complete chaos.

390
00:28:26,800 --> 00:28:27,900
Saengnuea

391
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:29,850
has already moved into that house.

392
00:28:32,860 --> 00:28:34,460
Really?

393
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:36,470
Yeah.

394
00:28:36,500 --> 00:28:39,100
After all,
he's already bonded with Naphitch.

395
00:28:42,660 --> 00:28:44,260
What about you? Are you okay?

396
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:49,060
I'm fine. I just need to get used to it.

397
00:28:49,550 --> 00:28:53,020
Now I'm already with Nakhin.

398
00:28:55,460 --> 00:28:56,260
Really?

399
00:29:00,080 --> 00:29:01,320
Finally.

400
00:29:02,600 --> 00:29:04,260
You finally have a boyfriend.

401
00:29:04,760 --> 00:29:06,020
Don't say it like that.

402
00:29:06,320 --> 00:29:08,720
It sounds like
you're asking for a beating.

403
00:29:11,330 --> 00:29:15,800
It's great, though.
Nakhin treats you so well.

404
00:29:16,400 --> 00:29:20,830
I guess.
It's just that he's a bit of a chuunibyou.

405
00:29:23,130 --> 00:29:24,530
He really is.

406
00:29:25,530 --> 00:29:27,130
But you can handle it.

407
00:29:28,100 --> 00:29:29,680
Didn't you like him a long time ago?

408
00:29:29,680 --> 00:29:30,280
Phatsa!

409
00:29:33,660 --> 00:29:36,530
What about you? Have you seen Nakhun yet?

410
00:29:39,780 --> 00:29:40,740
Not yet.

411
00:29:41,930 --> 00:29:43,730
My dad doesn't allow me to go out.

412
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:49,560
But he should be coming soon.

413
00:29:49,930 --> 00:29:50,860
How do you know?

414
00:29:56,160 --> 00:29:57,560
It's like I can smell him.

415
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:01,130
No need to guess anymore, then.

416
00:30:06,200 --> 00:30:07,100
Phatsa.

417
00:30:08,010 --> 00:30:08,810
Phatsa?

418
00:30:10,200 --> 00:30:11,330
Let's talk later

419
00:30:12,400 --> 00:30:13,400
I think he's here.

420
00:30:18,330 --> 00:30:19,260
You really came.

421
00:30:35,500 --> 00:30:36,730
I miss you so much.

422
00:30:38,800 --> 00:30:40,400
I haven't seen you in so long.

423
00:30:42,060 --> 00:30:44,190
The household has been so busy lately.

424
00:30:45,060 --> 00:30:46,700
But I miss you every day.

425
00:30:50,730 --> 00:30:53,100
I miss you too.

426
00:30:57,530 --> 00:30:59,260
Why are you acting like a child?

427
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:02,290
You've gone for so long.

428
00:31:07,660 --> 00:31:10,500
By the way, how's your arm?

429
00:31:12,760 --> 00:31:13,560
It's fine now.

430
00:31:13,710 --> 00:31:14,260
Look.

431
00:31:22,760 --> 00:31:24,200
I'm here to take you home.

432
00:31:25,930 --> 00:31:27,020
Home?

433
00:31:28,070 --> 00:31:28,870
Yeah.

434
00:31:29,560 --> 00:31:30,500
Back to our home.

435
00:31:33,460 --> 00:31:34,260
Really?

436
00:31:35,160 --> 00:31:35,960
Yes.

437
00:31:43,800 --> 00:31:45,000
You really missed me?

438
00:31:46,430 --> 00:31:47,230
I don't know.

439
00:31:47,920 --> 00:31:49,110
You don't?

440
00:31:50,650 --> 00:31:51,510
Do you know now?

441
00:31:52,800 --> 00:31:53,600
No.

442
00:31:56,960 --> 00:31:57,820
Tell me you did.

443
00:31:58,280 --> 00:31:59,080
Okay.

444
00:32:01,160 --> 00:32:02,760
I don't want you to leave yet.

445
00:32:05,150 --> 00:32:05,950
Dad.

446
00:32:14,760 --> 00:32:15,660
Sit properly.

447
00:32:28,530 --> 00:32:29,800
I told you not to leave.

448
00:32:33,900 --> 00:32:35,400
I'm not here just because

449
00:32:36,770 --> 00:32:38,920
I want to take him back,

450
00:32:41,330 --> 00:32:43,130
but because I must.

451
00:32:44,600 --> 00:32:45,400
Must?

452
00:32:45,940 --> 00:32:46,740
Yes.

453
00:32:48,260 --> 00:32:50,660
Because we've already completed our bond.

454
00:32:52,060 --> 00:32:53,260
And Phatsa's body

455
00:32:54,760 --> 00:32:56,930
is no longer like other Omegas

456
00:32:57,660 --> 00:32:58,800
since the bonding.

457
00:33:03,400 --> 00:33:05,130
Don't try to scare me with this.

458
00:33:06,400 --> 00:33:07,530
I'm not scaring you.

459
00:33:08,960 --> 00:33:10,220
I'm telling the truth.

460
00:33:13,600 --> 00:33:14,400
Phatsa and I

461
00:33:16,630 --> 00:33:18,760
can no longer be apart from each other.

462
00:33:20,330 --> 00:33:21,160
Because

463
00:33:22,700 --> 00:33:24,900
I've only been away from him for one day,

464
00:33:25,800 --> 00:33:29,360
and already I miss him so much
that I can't do anything at all.

465
00:33:34,130 --> 00:33:37,750
Are you sure

466
00:33:37,770 --> 00:33:40,700
these words aren't just
to take my son away?

467
00:33:41,100 --> 00:33:41,930
I'm sure.

468
00:33:45,300 --> 00:33:47,500
If anything ever happened to Phatsa...

469
00:33:48,300 --> 00:33:50,260
I will never let that happen.

470
00:33:51,800 --> 00:33:52,860
I love him.

471
00:33:58,960 --> 00:33:59,760
Fine,

472
00:33:59,780 --> 00:34:03,580
he's never really chosen anything
for himself since he was young.

473
00:34:06,800 --> 00:34:09,199
Forget it. You can go back with him.

474
00:34:11,659 --> 00:34:16,159
But I'm not handing my son over to you.

475
00:34:18,159 --> 00:34:18,960
Yes.

476
00:34:21,380 --> 00:34:25,480
That's enough.

477
00:34:29,500 --> 00:34:31,429
Don't get too excited.

478
00:34:31,449 --> 00:34:37,929
I'll be watching your every move.

479
00:34:38,760 --> 00:34:45,800
Yes, I have nothing to hide.

480
00:34:46,250 --> 00:34:47,050
Yes.

481
00:34:54,900 --> 00:34:59,930
♪ I've been trying to move a mountain
on my way to get to you ♪

482
00:35:00,510 --> 00:35:04,260
♪ Skinny dipping in an ocean ble ♪

483
00:35:05,740 --> 00:35:07,970
♪ It's an uphill kind of battle  ♪

484
00:35:07,970 --> 00:35:11,150
♪ To make you see my point of view ♪

485
00:35:11,440 --> 00:35:14,730
♪Is it worthy?
I ain't got a clue ♪

486
00:35:16,800 --> 00:35:20,480
♪ Ooh ♪

487
00:35:20,610 --> 00:35:24,520
♪ Say it isn't true ♪

488
00:35:24,550 --> 00:35:27,600
♪ Ooh ♪

489
00:35:27,630 --> 00:35:31,280
♪ Ooh ♪

490
00:35:31,310 --> 00:35:34,890
♪ Don't tel me I'm a fool ♪

491
00:35:34,920 --> 00:35:36,840
♪ Ooh ♪

492
00:35:36,860 --> 00:35:38,880
♪ A fool for you ♪

493
00:35:43,610 --> 00:35:47,190
♪ Ooh ♪

494
00:35:47,210 --> 00:35:52,640
♪ Say it isn't true ♪

495
00:35:52,670 --> 00:35:54,240
♪ Ooh ♪

496
00:35:54,260 --> 00:35:57,950
♪ Ooh ♪

497
00:35:57,980 --> 00:36:03,190
♪ Don't tel me I'm a fool ♪

498
00:36:03,220 --> 00:36:05,850
♪ A fool for you ♪

499
00:36:04,530 --> 00:36:06,130
I've checked this document.

500
00:36:06,360 --> 00:36:07,420
You can sign it now.

501
00:36:10,060 --> 00:36:10,860
Okay.

502
00:36:11,900 --> 00:36:13,800
I've rearranged the schedule.

503
00:36:14,730 --> 00:36:17,140
I've cancelled

504
00:36:17,160 --> 00:36:19,420
2 unimportant meetings this afternoon.

505
00:36:19,560 --> 00:36:22,620
The legal department is waiting
for the last document.

506
00:36:22,960 --> 00:36:26,130
I'll send it to them
as soon as you approve it.

507
00:36:31,460 --> 00:36:32,300
Okay.

508
00:36:34,100 --> 00:36:34,900
Okay.

509
00:36:41,300 --> 00:36:43,960
Once that document is handled,

510
00:36:43,980 --> 00:36:47,130
there are only 2 left,
and you can have a rest.

511
00:36:51,160 --> 00:36:52,500
Ever since I got you,

512
00:36:54,660 --> 00:36:56,390
my work has gotten much easier.

513
00:37:06,050 --> 00:37:07,310
Focus on you work.

514
00:37:08,330 --> 00:37:09,930
You're flirting with me now.

515
00:37:11,650 --> 00:37:13,570
If there’s nothing else,

516
00:37:13,600 --> 00:37:16,000
AI and I will deal with things outside.

517
00:37:17,930 --> 00:37:20,060
I'll arrange the rest of the schedule.

518
00:37:20,250 --> 00:37:22,050
I'll leave it to you.

519
00:37:22,970 --> 00:37:23,770
Okay.

520
00:37:38,260 --> 00:37:39,390
Are you almost done?

521
00:37:40,660 --> 00:37:41,460
Soon.

522
00:37:56,420 --> 00:38:02,350
Sign here and here.

523
00:38:03,930 --> 00:38:04,730
Where?

524
00:38:06,260 --> 00:38:07,060
Here.

525
00:38:15,100 --> 00:38:15,900
Where?

526
00:38:21,100 --> 00:38:21,900
Here.

527
00:38:26,300 --> 00:38:28,760
Here? Or here?

528
00:38:52,760 --> 00:38:53,760
Get back to work.

529
00:39:07,480 --> 00:39:09,210
It's already been made public like this.

530
00:39:07,610 --> 00:39:10,910
[In the next episode]

531
00:39:09,240 --> 00:39:11,160
I wonder
when we'll get to hear the good news.

532
00:39:11,160 --> 00:39:14,130
As long as Phatsa is willing,
even getting married tomorrow is fine.

533
00:39:14,130 --> 00:39:17,410
Don't let other people's opinions
override my heart.

534
00:39:17,520 --> 00:39:18,500
This way,

535
00:39:18,530 --> 00:39:21,020
we can finally be friends out in the open.

536
00:39:21,040 --> 00:39:24,340
You know, you're living like a joke?

537
00:39:24,640 --> 00:39:26,060
I don't care.

538
00:39:26,080 --> 00:39:27,410
No matter what happens,

539
00:39:27,410 --> 00:39:29,150
an Alpha always has a way out.

540
00:39:29,180 --> 00:39:31,000
And he still has the right to choose.

541
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:33,900
Why does everyone
keep talking about pregnancy lately?

542
00:39:33,900 --> 00:39:35,730
It's because you're so adorable.

543
00:39:35,730 --> 00:39:36,930
If you had a child,

544
00:39:36,960 --> 00:39:38,890
it would definitely be even cuter.

545
00:39:51,890 --> 00:39:55,810
♪ I linger in those beautiful memories ♪

546
00:39:55,840 --> 00:39:59,170
♪ I used to think we were meant to be ♪

547
00:39:59,490 --> 00:40:01,110
♪ But I also know ♪

548
00:40:01,140 --> 00:40:05,030
♪ That reality isn't like that ♪

549
00:40:05,150 --> 00:40:09,450
♪ I tried so hard to keep you
from leaving ♪

550
00:40:09,470 --> 00:40:12,900
♪ But this broken love
is already shattered ♪

551
00:40:12,920 --> 00:40:15,360
♪ Because I always believed
you would stay ♪

552
00:40:15,390 --> 00:40:19,360
♪ Everything I have,
I'd give it up for you ♪

553
00:40:19,450 --> 00:40:22,260
♪ Had the best days ahead of us ♪

554
00:40:22,290 --> 00:40:25,270
♪ Turns out there are
no more days left ♪

555
00:40:25,290 --> 00:40:28,280
♪ For us ♪

556
00:40:28,310 --> 00:40:31,220
♪ What's left to stay in my mind ♪

557
00:40:31,250 --> 00:40:36,230
♪ How many more times do I have to hurt
to understand ♪

558
00:40:36,490 --> 00:40:39,470
♪ How much longer do I have to cry ♪

559
00:40:39,500 --> 00:40:44,210
♪ Before my heart tells me
it's time to let go ♪

560
00:40:44,230 --> 00:40:49,800
